## Implementation
`bowling.py:1` — replaced the stub with `BowlingGame`:
- `roll(pins)` appends each throw to `self.rolls`.
- `score()` walks the roll list once over 10 frames: strike → `10 + next two`, spare → `10 + next roll`, open → `pins`; the same index walk naturally consumes 10th-frame fill balls.

